#version 460

// 09 UPDATE FILM - COMPENSATED MEAN. Folds each pixel's K radiance slots into sums instead of a running
// mean, and resolves the mean from them. Runs once per frame, after the bounce loop.
//
// Per pixel it keeps (binding 31, 48 bytes, crt_film.glsl): sum(w L) per channel and sum(w), each a
// Neumaier-compensated float sum, so that the mean keeps its precision out to the sample counts where
// a running mean's float stalls (pbrt measures its error flattening after about 1000 samples with
// a 32-bit pixel); Welford's mean and M2 of the luminance, for the standard error of the mean; and the
// number of samples accepted. A sample is weighed by the sign kernel 00 left in the slot's w: +1 for
// every filter that is never negative, so the mean is then the plain mean of the samples, and -1 where
// Mitchell's or Lanczos's filter is negative, pbrt's weighted estimator (PBR 4ed equation 5.13).
// The clamp, when set, scales a sample down to the threshold before it is summed (pbrt's maxComponentValue).
//
// It writes the resolved mean into the accumulation image every frame, so the tonemap, the reference
// comparison and the analysis views read the image they always did.
//
// The film's count of samples TAKEN (binding 9) is advanced by every slot that spawned, accepted or
// dropped, while the count of samples accepted is in the record. Kernel 00 and the samplers seed a path
// from the count taken, so a sample dropped as non-finite is not drawn again next frame: 0901 advances
// by the accepted samples only, and at one sample per frame a pixel that dropped one never got past
// it (docs/plans/completed/pbrt-verification-harness.md, finding 7). The drops are counted into
// traversalStats[CRT_STAT_DROPPED_SAMPLES], as in 0901.
//
// docs/plans/completed/pbrt-film-and-reconstruction.md.

#extension GL_GOOGLE_include_directive : require
#include "include/crt_common.glsl"
#include "include/crt_film.glsl"
#include "include/crt_aov.glsl"
#include "include/crt_film_update.glsl"
